; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Flow Field
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     flow field, vector field, SIN, COS, particles, generative
; SUMMARY:  Releases hundreds of particles that drift along an invisible field of directions, leaving silky trails.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Imagine every point on the screen has an arrow telling you which
;   way to go, like wind or water currents. The arrows here come from
;   a formula mixing sine waves, so nearby arrows point almost the
;   same way. Particles start at random spots and follow the arrows
;   for a while, drawing a thin line. Hundreds of lines together
;   show the shape of the invisible currents.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Each run picks new starting points and a new random
;   twist for the field. Change :particles and :life for denser or
;   longer trails.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a vector field: a heading computed from x and y
;   * combining several SIN and COS waves to make smooth patterns
;   * random seeds for the field's "personality"
;   * stopping a particle when it leaves the screen
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change the numbers 0.9 and 1.3 in FIELD.HEADING.
;   * Color trails by their starting height instead of by x.
;   * Make the particles start in a circle around the middle.
; ============================================================

; FIELD.HEADING outputs the direction of the current at (x, y).
; Small multipliers like 0.9 make big, slow swirls; larger ones make
; small, tight swirls. :twist changes from run to run.
to field.heading :x :y
  output :twist + 120 * (sin (:x * 0.9 + :y * 0.3)) ~
               + 90 * (cos (:y * 1.3 - :x * 0.4 + :twist))
end

; ON.SCREEN? is true while the point is inside the turtle world.
to on.screen? :x :y
  output and (abs :x) < 400 (abs :y) < 300
end

; DRIFT lets one particle follow the field from a random point.
to drift
  penup
  setxy (random -400 400) (random -300 300)
  ; Color depends on where it starts: warm on the left, cool on the
  ; right, so the picture has a gentle color sweep.
  localmake "mix (xcor + 400) / 800
  setpencolor (list 250 - 170 * :mix 120 + 60 * :mix 90 + 160 * :mix)
  pendown
  repeat :life [
    if not on.screen? xcor ycor [stop]
    setheading field.heading xcor ycor
    forward 3
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [14 16 26]
make "twist random 360
make "particles 350
make "life 60
setpensize 1.2
repeat :particles [drift]
